#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:43
msgid ""
"image:araby/logo.webp[width=94,height=84,float=\"right\"] The land of Araby "
"lies along the north west coast of the Southlands between the Atalan "
"mountains and the Great Ocean. To the east is the Great Desert that "
"separates Araby from the Lands of the Dead. Although the climate is dry and "
"hot the western winds carry moisture laden clouds that give up their water "
"as they are suddenly forced upwards by tall Atalan peaks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:54
msgid ""
"The Arabians are great sailors and have for many centuries fished the "
"adjoining seas and traded south along the coast, northwards to the Old "
"World, and westwards as far as Ulthuan.  The High Elves do not permit "
"Arabian vessels to travel further west than Ulthuan itself, their high-"
"prowed dhows are a common sight in the outer harbours of Lothern. For their "
"part the High Elves maintain a mercantile presence in Copher and Lashiek as "
"they have since time immemorial. The Elves and men of Araby had dealings "
"even during the long centuries when the Elves abandoned the Old World."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:66
msgid ""
"The mostly densely populated part of Araby lies to the north of the River of "
"the Serpent; the largest waterway in the land and one of the few rivers that "
"flows all year long. This land is home to four great cities: Lashiek, "
"Copher, Martek, and Alhaka or (as it is sometimes rendered) Al-haikk which "
"means City of Thieves in the Arabian tongue. Each of these cities and the "
"surrounding lands forms an independent principality ruled over by a Sultan "
"or Caliph. South of the River of Serpents the land is not so fertile and the "
"terrain is much dryer. East of the Atalan mountains the great desert "
"stretches for hundreds of miles towards the Land of the Dead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:78
msgid ""
"Araby lies far from the world’s poles and therefore from the ultimate source "
"of the magical winds that blow from the north.  As a result magic that is "
"common in the Old World is far more diffuse in Araby so it is much more "
"difficult for sorcerers to work their spellcraft. Arabian magic has "
"therefore developed quite differently than that of other men. Arabian "
"sorcerers use their powers to control elemental spirits of the desert, "
"djinn, efreets, genies and such-like spirits. These spirits are worshipped "
"by the superstitious people of Araby. It is commonly believed that the "
"spirits must be appeased with prayers and small tokens of respect such as "
"gifts of food and drink."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:87
msgid ""
"The rulers of Araby maintain their own armies based upon the great cities "
"and tributary tribes that live in the surrounding lands. The leaders of "
"these tribes are called Emirs or, amongst the desert tribes of the south and "
"east, Sheiks. The rules of cities and their surrounding lands are called "
"Sultans and the Sultan of Alhaka is the acknowledged overlord of all the "
"other cities of Araby. In consequence he is also known as the Great Sultan – "
"the ruler of all Araby."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:101
msgid ""
"The Sultans are proud of their troops and especially of their cavalry. It is "
"popularly supposed that the horses of Araby are descended from Elven horses "
"brought over from the west many centuries ago. They are graceful and swift "
"creatures and very highly valued. The very best of the Arabian foot-solders "
"are also well equipped, with steel armour, keen tulwars, gleaming helmets, "
"and fine silk clothing. These household troops or guards accompany the "
"Sultans when they travel beyond the grounds of their magnificent palaces. "
"The loyalty of these troops is famous. They are amply rewarded with riches, "
"luxuries, and prestige as a result. As well as these regular and garrison "
"troops there are the irregular fighters from the desert tribes, including "
"camel mounted warriors from the lands to the south and east."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid "Araby army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$araby.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. 5: Remove extra initial .
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[guards,†1]]1. Guards"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:127
msgid ""
"The Sultan’s Guards are so unquestioningly loyal that they will obey the "
"first order given to them each turn on the Command roll of 10 or less so "
"long as the order comes from the General himself. No penalties are applied "
"to this order.  Further orders are given using the General’s normal command "
"value and penalties. This applies only to Guards and not to brigades that "
"include Guards and other units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[desert-riders,†2]]2. Desert Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:133
msgid ""
"Desert Riders have a shooting range of 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this "
"unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading and "
"shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit still "
"needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[camel-riders,†3]]3. Camel Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:142
msgid ""
"Camel Riders ignore distance modifiers when commands are issued to them. "
"This applies only to Camel Riders and not to brigades that include Camel "
"Riders and other units. Remember that characters are still bound by their "
"maximum command ranges and cannot issue orders to units beyond range. This "
"represents their fierce self-reliance and their mounts’ instinctive sense of "
"direction allowing them to operate effectively far from their own battle "
"lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:148
msgid ""
"Because Camels are such intractable creatures all orders are issued with a "
"Command penalty of −1, this penalty applies to any unit of Camel Riders or "
"to any brigade that contains one or more units of Camel Riders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:149
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[magic-carpets,†4]]4. Magic Carpets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:157
msgid ""
"Magic carpets can fly – they have been rated as aerial ‘cavalry’ as this is "
"the closest categorisation to their type. Because they are awkward flyers, "
"they can be pursued by any type of enemy troops. They have a shooting range "
"of 15cm and 360° vision – stands in this unit can draw line of sight from "
"all edges for the purpose of evading and shooting, including shooting at "
"charging enemies. Note that this unit still needs Line of Sight from its "
"front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[elephants,†5]]5. Elephants"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:166
msgid ""
"Elephants cause terror. Elephants cannot be brigaded with cavalry but can be "
"brigaded with other types of troops including other Elephants. If an "
"Elephant unit would otherwise become confused – for whatever reason – then "
"it will stampede instead. It is not confused and none of the normal rules "
"for confusion apply. Stampeding elephants automatically cease to stampede at "
"the end of their Command phase (note that this is in the same way as "
"confused units cease to be confused)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:172
msgid ""
"Stampeding Elephants cannot be given orders or use initiative. Instead roll "
"a dice at the start of the Command phase before moving anything else on "
"initiative, and move the unit as follows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:199
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"h|1–2\n"
"|Move towards the nearest enemy unit as far as possible – if\n"
"the stampeding elephants contact the enemy they automatically\n"
"count as charging even if they couldn’t see at the start of the\n"
"move. If the elephant contacts a friendly unit it counts as moving\n"
"into friends (see below).\n"
"\n"
"h|3–4\n"
"|Move directly away from the nearest enemy unit as far as\n"
"possible – work out the stampede direction in the same way as you\n"
"would for an evade move. If the elephant contacts another enemy\n"
"unit it counts as charging (see above). If the elephant contacts a\n"
"friendly unit it counts as moving into friends (see below).\n"
"\n"
"h|5\n"
"|Move towards the nearest friendly unit as far as possible – if the\n"
"stampeding elephants contact the friendly unit they automatically\n"
"count as charging even if they couldn’t see at the start of the move.\n"
"\n"
"h|6\n"
"|Move directly away from the nearest friendly unit as far as\n"
"possible – work out the stampede direction in the same way as\n"
"you would for an evade move. If the elephant contacts an enemy\n"
"or friendly unit it counts as charging (see above).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:211
msgid ""
"A Stampeding Elephant unit that charges into an enemy or friendly unit "
"fights in the combat phase in the same way as a regular charging unit. The "
"stampeding Elephant counts as ‘enemies’ for the duration of the combat and "
"therefore continue to cause ‘terror’ in opponents regardless of which side "
"they are on. The Elephants count as charging in the first round.  If the "
"Elephants win a combat round then they must pursue if possible and will "
"continue to do so each round. Should their opponents be destroyed they will "
"not advance but will halt without reforming."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:220
msgid ""
"Stampeding Elephants might conceivably move into a unit, therefore "
"initiating combat, but are unable to form a battleline because they have "
"insufficient movement distance. In the case of stampeding elephants, the "
"combat is still fought, and the elephants still count as charging. It is up "
"to the player whether he moves the elephants the extra distance required to "
"make a battle-line or simply fights with the elephants in an irregular "
"formation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:222
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[flying-carpet,†6]]6. Flying Carpet"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:223
msgid "This is considered to be a flying chariot mount."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:224
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[elephant,†7]]7. Elephant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:227
msgid ""
"The Elephant mount is a standard monster mount except that a character "
"mounted on an Elephant cannot join a unit of friendly cavalry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:230
msgid "A unit joined by a character riding an Elephant causes Terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:231
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[djinn,†8]]8. Djinn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:235
msgid ""
"The Djinn accompanies its master and can transform both of them into a "
"whirlwind enabling the stand to fly as for a normal flying mount. If the "
"sorcerer has a Djinn he can also cast the <<curse-of-the-djinn>>) spell with "
"a +1 casting bonus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:240
msgid ""
"Note that unusually the Djinn has +2 shooting attacks – these are added to a "
"stand from a unit that the character has joined and can only be used when "
"the character joins a unit (see xref:rules:characters.adoc#characters-that-"
"shoot[Characters that shoot])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:244
msgid ""
"If the Wizard is accompanied by a Djinn then any unit he joins causes Terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:251
#, no-wrap
msgid "Araby spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:254
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sand Storm"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:260
msgid ""
"_The sorcerer commands the desert spirits to engulf his foes in a swirling "
"cloud of choking sand and dust._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:264
msgid ""
"The spell is cast upon the Sorcerer himself and affects all enemy units "
"within 30cm of the stand. The spell lasts until the end of the opposing "
"player’s following turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:270
msgid ""
"The spell affects the opposing army’s ability to issue commands.  All enemy "
"units within 30cm of the Arabian Sorcerer suffer a −1 Command penalty. This "
"penalty is applied when each order is issued. For example, a unit might "
"therefore be within 30cm of the Sorcerer for one order but not for a second, "
"for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mirage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:275
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:197
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/dark-elves.adoc:257
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/lizardmen.adoc:262
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:235
msgid "[.cost]#4+ to cast# [.points]#Range 60cm#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:278
msgid ""
"_The sorcerer creates the illusion of a huge host of fearsome warriors, "
"bearing down inexorably upon his startled foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:294
msgid ""
"To use this spell the player will need an additional unit chosen from the "
"Araby list – this can be infantry, cavalry or monsters it does not matter "
"which. This unit becomes the ‘illusion’ and is immediately placed within "
"60cm of the sorcerer and more than 20cm from any enemy units. The "
"illusionary unit cannot move or fight – for it isn’t really there! However, "
"the illusionary unit is treated as if it were real by the enemy up until "
"such time as an enemy unit charges into contact with it, touches it as an "
"incidental contact during combat, advances upon it, or brings it into combat "
"in any other fashion. This means, for example, Command penalties are "
"suffered for proximity, and enemy shooters are obliged to target the "
"illusion if it is the closest target – it cannot be harmed of course! The "
"illusionary unit is also dispelled immediately if the Araby player moves any "
"of his units or characters through it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:299
msgid ""
"Whilst the Mirage unit is on the battlefield the Wizard cannot cast any "
"other spells – if the player wishes the Wizard to cast a new spell the "
"Mirage comes to an end and the Wizard can then attempt a new spell as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:301
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sunstrike"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:307
msgid ""
"_Bright beams of burning energy leap from the sorcerer’s eyes and scythe "
"through all before him._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:318
msgid ""
"Draw an imaginary line 30cm long from the Wizard’s stand in any direction "
"you wish. Each unit under the line takes three shooting attacks worked out "
"in the usual way all relevant modifiers are applied. Note that this spell "
"can easily affect several units and will affect all units that fall beneath "
"its path (including you own). Unengaged units can be driven back by "
"Sunstrike as with ordinary shooting whether friend or foe.  Engaged units "
"cannot be driven back but carry over any hits that are scored into the first "
"round of combat. Hits caused by the Sunstrike count as having been struck in "
"the combat itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:320
#, no-wrap
msgid "Curse of the Djinn"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:326
msgid ""
"_The Sorcerer channels the immense power of the Djinn through his own body "
"and lays a terrible curse upon his foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:330
msgid ""
"The Sorcerer may cast this spell on an enemy unit within range.  The target "
"unit must re-roll all successful armour saves for the duration of the "
"following close combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/araby.adoc:333
msgid ""
"If the Sorcerer has a Djinn then he adds +1 to his dice roll when casting "
"this spell, and therefore casts successfully on a 5+."
msgstr ""
